{%- comment -%}
  HooknLoop — Order confirmation
  ==============================
  Paste into: Settings > Notifications > Order confirmation > Edit code.

  DESIGN NOTE
  A works docket, not a lifestyle receipt. These buyers are trades, workshops
  and procurement people who read dockets and invoices all day, and HooknLoop's
  own product labels are engineering spec cards — checkbox grids, HOOK / LOOP,
  percentage ticks. So every piece of DATA here is monospace (order number,
  quantities, money, addresses) and only the prose is proportional. Numbers land
  in columns that scan, and the register matches the paperwork this order will
  sit beside.

  One flare: the 6px orange band under the masthead, which reads as a strip of
  the product laid across the page. Everything else stays navy and grey so that
  band and the CTA are the only things that raise their voice.

  DELIBERATELY ABSENT
  No estimated delivery date. That was removed at the source (Settings >
  Shipping and delivery > Estimated delivery dates = Off) because the manual
  range promised up to 22 Aug on metro orders. Do not reintroduce it here — a
  date in the email that the warehouse cannot hit costs more than no date.

  SCOPE
  Handles single-shipment orders of simple products, which is every order this
  store takes. It does NOT handle bundles, nested line items or split carts the
  way Shopify's stock template does. If those are ever sold, revisit.

  Editing this marks the notification as customised, so it stops inheriting
  Shopify's future updates to this email. That is the trade for controlling it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light only">
  <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light only">
  <title>Order {{ order_name }} confirmed</title>
  <style type="text/css">
    body,table,td,a { -webkit-text-size-adjust:100%; -ms-text-size-adjust:100%; }
    table,td { mso-table-lspace:0pt; mso-table-rspace:0pt; }
    img { -ms-interpolation-mode:bicubic; border:0; height:auto; line-height:100%; outline:none; text-decoration:none; }
    body { margin:0 !important; padding:0 !important; width:100% !important; background:#f4f7fb; }
    a { color:#b8460a; }

    /* The docket collapses to one column on a phone. Addresses stack rather
       than shrink, because a squeezed address is a misread address. */
    @media only screen and (max-width:600px){
      .full { width:100% !important; }
      .px   { padding-left:22px !important; padding-right:22px !important; }
      .stack { display:block !important; width:100% !important; }
      .stack-gap { height:22px !important; line-height:22px !important; font-size:22px !important; }
      .btn a { display:block !important; text-align:center !important; }
      .h1 { font-size:27px !important; line-height:1.18 !important; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0; padding:0; background:#f4f7fb;">

  {%- comment -%} Preheader: the inbox preview line. Says the one thing worth knowing. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div style="display:none; font-size:1px; line-height:1px; max-height:0; max-width:0; opacity:0; overflow:hidden; mso-hide:all; color:#f4f7fb;">
    Order {{ order_name }} is confirmed. We're getting it ready to ship — tracking follows shortly.
  </div>

  <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#f4f7fb;">
    <tr>
      <td align="center" style="padding:0 12px;">

        <table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" class="full"
               style="width:600px; max-width:600px; margin:26px 0; background:#ffffff; border-radius:14px; overflow:hidden;">

          <!-- ══ MASTHEAD ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
          {%- comment -%}
            White, not navy, and that is the logo's decision rather than a
            preference. The HooknLoop mark is royal blue with an orange "n" and
            a grey .COM.AU — drawn for white. On a navy field the blue letters
            sink into the background and the grey domain disappears entirely.
            A masthead that hides the logo is not a masthead, so the field is
            white and the orange rule below carries the separation instead.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <tr>
            <td style="background:#ffffff; padding:26px 30px 22px;" class="px">
              <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
                <tr>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    shop.email_logo_url is whatever is set under Settings >
                    Notifications > branding. It is empty on this store, which
                    is why the masthead came through blank — and the theme logo
                    is no help because it is an SVG, which Gmail and Outlook
                    both refuse to render.

                    So the fallback is a real PNG from Shopify Files
                    (logo_5.png, 389x69, blue-on-white) hardcoded here. The
                    Shopify setting still wins if it is ever filled in; this
                    only guarantees the masthead is never empty again.

                    Served at 180px wide from a 389px source, so it stays sharp
                    on retina. width/height are attributes as well as CSS
                    because Outlook ignores the CSS.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <td align="left" valign="middle">
                    {%- if shop.email_logo_url %}
                      <img src="{{ shop.email_logo_url }}" alt="{{ shop.name }}" width="{{ shop.email_logo_width | default: 180 }}" style="display:block; max-width:200px; border:0;">
                    {%- else %}
                      <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0975/4509/3489/files/logo_5.png?v=1767767497"
                           alt="HooknLoop" width="180" height="32"
                           style="display:block; width:180px; height:32px; border:0;">
                    {%- endif %}
                  </td>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    The order number is the datum a trade buyer quotes back to us
                    on the phone, so it is set like a job number — mono, right,
                    with a quiet label above it — not buried in the body copy.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <td align="right" valign="middle">
                    <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:9.5px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.16em; color:#5a6b8c; text-transform:uppercase;">Order</div>
                    <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:17px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.02em; color:#142548; padding-top:3px;">{{ order_name }}</div>
                    {%- if po_number %}
                      <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:10px; color:#5a6b8c; padding-top:4px;">PO {{ po_number }}</div>
                    {%- endif %}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </td>
          </tr>

          {%- comment -%}
            A hairline, not the orange band that was here. The band was meant to
            read as a strip of tape laid across the docket, but at full width and
            6px it fought the logo for attention the moment the eye landed —
            the first thing seen should be the mark, not a stripe under it.

            A 1px rule in the same grey as the table hairlines below does the
            one job actually needed: separating the masthead from the message.
            That leaves the CTA as the only orange on the page, which is where
            the emphasis belongs.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <tr><td style="border-top:1px solid #e7ecf4; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</td></tr>

          <!-- ══ MESSAGE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:30px 30px 0;" class="px">
              <h1 class="h1" style="margin:0; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:31px; line-height:1.14; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:-0.02em; color:#142548;">
                {%- if customer.first_name -%}Thanks, {{ customer.first_name }} —{%- else -%}Thanks —{%- endif -%}<br>your order is confirmed.
              </h1>

              <p style="margin:15px 0 0; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.62; color:#5a6b8c;">
                {%- if has_pending_payment -%}
                  {%- if buyer_action_required -%}
                    We'll confirm your order as soon as your payment completes.
                  {%- else -%}
                    Your payment is processing. We'll email you the moment it clears.
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- elsif payment_charged_on_fulfillment -%}
                  We've received your order. Your payment method is charged when the order is ready to go out, and we'll let you know when it ships.
                {%- elsif requires_shipping -%}
                  {%- case delivery_method -%}
                    {%- when 'pick-up' -%}
                      We're getting your order ready. You'll get an email when it's ready to collect.
                    {%- when 'local' -%}
                      We're getting your order ready for delivery.
                    {%- else -%}
                      We're getting your order ready to ship. You'll get tracking as soon as it's on its way.
                  {%- endcase -%}
                {%- else -%}
                  We're processing your order now.
                {%- endif -%}
              </p>

              {%- if delivery_instructions != blank %}
                <p style="margin:14px 0 0; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5a6b8c;">
                  <strong style="color:#142548;">Delivery notes:</strong> {{ delivery_instructions }}
                </p>
              {%- endif %}

              {%- comment -%}
                Manual payment instructions — bank transfer details and the
                like. Shopify's original renders these as a bare table; here
                they get the same panel treatment as the tracking number,
                because if an order is waiting on a transfer these numbers are
                the single most important thing in the email.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- for transaction in transactions %}
                {%- if transaction.show_buyer_pending_payment_instructions? %}
                  <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#f4f7fb; border-radius:12px; margin-top:18px;">
                    <tr>
                      <td style="padding:18px 20px;">
                        <div style="font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#142548;">{{ transaction.buyer_pending_payment_notice }}</div>
                        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin-top:12px; font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:12.5px;">
                          {%- for instruction in transaction.buyer_pending_payment_instructions %}
                            <tr>
                              <td style="padding:4px 0; color:#5a6b8c;">{{ instruction.header }}</td>
                              <td align="right" style="padding:4px 0; color:#142548; font-weight:700;">{{ instruction.value }}</td>
                            </tr>
                          {%- endfor %}
                          <tr>
                            <td style="padding:4px 0; color:#5a6b8c;">Amount</td>
                            <td align="right" style="padding:4px 0; color:#142548; font-weight:700;">{{ transaction.amount | money }}</td>
                          </tr>
                        </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                {%- endif %}
              {%- endfor %}

              {%- comment -%}
                Gift cards are emailed separately, so the order confirmation
                says so rather than leaving someone hunting for a code that was
                never in this message.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign gift_card_line_items = line_items | where: "gift_card" -%}
              {%- assign found_gift_card_with_recipient_email = false -%}
              {%- for line_item in gift_card_line_items -%}
                {%- if line_item.properties["__shopify_send_gift_card_to_recipient"] and line_item.properties["Recipient email"] -%}
                  {%- assign found_gift_card_with_recipient_email = true -%}
                  {%- break -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- if found_gift_card_with_recipient_email %}
                <p style="margin:14px 0 0; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5a6b8c;">Your gift card recipient will get an email with their code.</p>
              {%- elsif gift_card_line_items.first %}
                <p style="margin:14px 0 0; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5a6b8c;">You'll get a separate email for any gift cards.</p>
              {%- endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>

          <!-- ══ CTA ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:22px 30px 0;" class="px">
              <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" class="btn">
                <tr>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    "Track your order" is deliberate.

                    Nothing has shipped when this email sends, so there is no
                    tracking behind the link yet. But order_status_url is a
                    permanent page, and this email is the only place the
                    customer will ever have that link — they come back to it
                    days later, once there IS tracking on it. Labelling it for
                    the moment it is sent would be labelling it for the least
                    important visit.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <td align="center" bgcolor="#e87722" style="border-radius:10px;">
                    <a href="{{ order_status_url | default: shop.url }}"
                       style="display:inline-block; padding:15px 30px; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15.5px; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:0.005em; color:#142548; text-decoration:none; border-radius:10px;">
                      Track your order &rarr;
                    </a>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <!-- ══ ORDER DOCKET ══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:30px 30px 0;" class="px">
              <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
                     style="border-top:2px solid #142548;">
                {%- for line in subtotal_line_items %}
                  <tr>
                    <td valign="top" width="62" style="padding:15px 14px 15px 0; border-bottom:1px solid #e7ecf4;">
                      {%- if line.image %}
                        <img src="{{ line | img_url: 'compact_cropped' }}" width="62" height="62" alt="" style="display:block; width:62px; height:62px; border-radius:8px; background:#f4f7fb;">
                      {%- else %}
                        <div style="width:62px; height:62px; border-radius:8px; background:#f4f7fb;">&nbsp;</div>
                      {%- endif %}
                    </td>
                    <td valign="top" style="padding:15px 12px 15px 0; border-bottom:1px solid #e7ecf4;">
                      <div style="font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; font-weight:700; line-height:1.4; color:#142548;">
                        {{ line.title | default: line.product.title }}
                      </div>
                      {%- if line.variant.title and line.variant.title != 'Default Title' %}
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:11.5px; color:#5a6b8c; padding-top:5px;">{{ line.variant.title }}</div>
                      {%- endif %}
                      {%- if line.selling_plan_allocation %}
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:11.5px; color:#5a6b8c; padding-top:4px;">{{ line.selling_plan_allocation.selling_plan.name }}</div>
                      {%- endif %}
                      {%- for discount_allocation in line.discount_allocations %}
                        {%- if discount_allocation.discount_application.target_selection != 'all' %}
                          <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:11px; font-weight:700; color:#1a8449; padding-top:5px;">
                            {{ discount_allocation.discount_application.title | upcase }} &minus;{{ discount_allocation.amount | money }}
                          </div>
                        {%- endif %}
                      {%- endfor %}
                      {%- comment -%}
                        Line item properties — cut-to-length notes, uploaded
                        files, anything captured on the product page. This store
                        offers custom cutting, so these carry real instructions
                        and have to survive into the confirmation.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      {%- for property in line.properties -%}
                        {%- assign property_first_char = property.first | slice: 0 -%}
                        {%- if property.last != blank and property_first_char != '_' %}
                          <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:11.5px; line-height:1.55; color:#5a6b8c; padding-top:5px;">
                            <span style="color:#142548;">{{ property.first }}:</span>
                            {% if property.last contains '/uploads/' %}<a href="{{ property.last }}" style="color:#b8460a;">{{ property.last | split: '/' | last }}</a>{% else %}{{ property.last }}{% endif %}
                          </div>
                        {%- endif %}
                      {%- endfor %}

                      {%- if line.refunded_quantity > 0 %}
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:10.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.1em; color:#8a3a0c; text-transform:uppercase; padding-top:6px;">Refunded &times;{{ line.refunded_quantity }}</div>
                      {%- endif %}

                      {%- comment -%} Quantity reads as a multiplier, the way a packing slip writes it. {%- endcomment -%}
                      <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:12px; font-weight:700; color:#142548; padding-top:7px;">&times;&nbsp;{{ line.quantity }}</div>
                    </td>
                    <td valign="top" align="right" style="padding:15px 0; border-bottom:1px solid #e7ecf4; white-space:nowrap;">
                      {%- if line.original_line_price != line.final_line_price %}
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:12px; color:#8194b5; text-decoration:line-through;">{{ line.original_line_price | money }}</div>
                      {%- endif %}
                      <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:14.5px; font-weight:700; color:#142548; padding-top:2px;">
                        {%- if line.final_line_price > 0 -%}{{ line.final_line_price | money }}{%- else -%}Free{%- endif -%}
                      </div>
                      {%- comment -%}
                        Unit pricing — "$4.20 / m" and the like. Tape sold by
                        the metre is exactly what this filter exists for, so it
                        stays rather than being dropped as an edge case.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      {%- if line.unit_price_measurement %}
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:11px; color:#5a6b8c; padding-top:4px;">
                          {{ line.unit_price | unit_price_with_measurement: line.unit_price_measurement }}
                        </div>
                      {%- endif %}
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                {%- endfor %}
              </table>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <!-- ══ TOTALS ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:18px 30px 0;" class="px">
              <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
                     style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:13.5px; color:#5a6b8c;">
                {%- comment -%}
                  Every line Shopify's own template shows, kept in the same
                  order. The design changed; the accounting did not. Each row is
                  conditional, so an order with no duties or no discount simply
                  omits those lines rather than printing a row of zeros.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <tr>
                  <td style="padding:5px 0;">Subtotal</td>
                  <td align="right" style="padding:5px 0; color:#142548;">{{ subtotal_price | money }}</td>
                </tr>

                {%- comment -%}
                  Discount codes are named, because "-$5.00" with no code is the
                  line people query. Line-item discounts already appear on their
                  item, so only order-wide and shipping ones are repeated here.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- for discount_application in discount_applications %}
                  {%- if discount_application.total_allocated_amount > 0 and discount_application.target_selection != 'explicit' %}
                    <tr>
                      <td style="padding:5px 0; color:#1a8449;">
                        Discount
                        {%- if discount_application.title %} <span style="font-weight:700;">{{ discount_application.title | upcase }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                      </td>
                      <td align="right" style="padding:5px 0; color:#1a8449; font-weight:700;">&minus;{{ discount_application.total_allocated_amount | money }}</td>
                    </tr>
                  {%- endif %}
                {%- endfor %}

                {%- if requires_shipping %}
                  <tr>
                    <td style="padding:5px 0;">Shipping{% if shipping_method %} &middot; {{ shipping_method.title }}{% endif %}</td>
                    <td align="right" style="padding:5px 0; color:#142548;">
                      {%- if shipping_price > 0 -%}{{ shipping_price | money }}{%- else -%}Free{%- endif -%}
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                {%- endif %}

                {%- if total_duties %}
                  <tr>
                    <td style="padding:5px 0;">Duties</td>
                    <td align="right" style="padding:5px 0; color:#142548;">{{ total_duties | money }}</td>
                  </tr>
                {%- endif %}

                {%- comment -%}
                  One "Taxes" line, not a row per tax_line.

                  Looping tax_lines is right for the US, where an order can
                  carry State Tax, County Tax and City Tax that a buyer may need
                  itemised. Australian orders carry a single GST, so the loop
                  produced one row either way — but named inconsistently, and it
                  would start splitting into State/County rows the moment a US
                  order came through. The live email this replaces shows a
                  single "Taxes" line; this keeps that.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  "Includes GST", not "Taxes", when tax is inclusive.

                  Every order on this store is taxes_included: true — subtotal
                  plus shipping already equals the total, and GST sits inside
                  it. A row labelled "Taxes" in a column of numbers that add up
                  to the total reads as an extra charge, and a trade buyer
                  checking the arithmetic finds it does not add up.

                  Naming the tax line ("Includes GST $3.31") also gives business
                  customers the figure they need for BAS without opening the
                  invoice. Falls back to plain "Taxes" if tax is ever charged on
                  top, which is what an export order would do.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if tax_price > 0 %}
                  <tr>
                    <td style="padding:5px 0;">
                      {%- if taxes_included -%}
                        Includes {{ tax_lines.first.title | default: 'tax' }}
                      {%- else -%}
                        Taxes
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </td>
                    <td align="right" style="padding:5px 0; color:#142548;">{{ tax_price | money }}</td>
                  </tr>
                {%- endif %}

                <tr><td colspan="2" style="padding-top:9px;"><div style="border-top:2px solid #142548; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</div></td></tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="padding:11px 0 0; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-weight:800; color:#142548;">Total</td>
                  <td align="right" style="padding:11px 0 0; font-size:20px; font-weight:700; color:#142548;">{{ total_price | money_with_currency }}</td>
                </tr>

                {%- if total_discounts > 0 %}
                  <tr>
                    <td colspan="2" align="right" style="padding:7px 0 0; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13.5px; font-weight:700; color:#1a8449;">
                      You saved {{ total_discounts | money }}
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                {%- endif %}

                {%- comment -%}
                  Only shown when it differs from the total — on a deposit or a
                  partial payment, "total paid today" is the number the customer
                  needs, and repeating it when it equals the total is noise.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if total_paid and total_paid != total_price %}
                  <tr><td colspan="2" style="padding-top:9px;"><div style="border-top:1px solid #e7ecf4; font-size:0; line-height:0;">&nbsp;</div></td></tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td style="padding:10px 0 0; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-weight:700; color:#142548;">Total paid today</td>
                    <td align="right" style="padding:10px 0 0; font-size:15px; font-weight:700; color:#142548;">{{ total_paid | money_with_currency }}</td>
                  </tr>
                {%- endif %}

                {%- comment -%}
                  Shopify's original repeats the card here as a per-transaction
                  breakdown — "Visa ending in 4242 · $519.18" — and then again
                  under Customer information. That breakdown exists to split a
                  payment across two methods (gift card plus card, or two
                  cards). Every order this store takes is a single payment, so
                  it was printing the same card twice for no added information.

                  The card now appears once, under Customer information, where
                  someone reconciling a statement looks for it. If split
                  payments ever start happening, restore the loop here — that is
                  the case it was written for.
                {%- endcomment -%}
              </table>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <!-- ══ ADDRESSES ═════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:30px 30px 34px;" class="px">
              <div style="border-top:1px solid #e7ecf4; padding-top:24px;">
                <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
                  <tr>
                    {%- if requires_shipping and shipping_address %}
                      <td class="stack" valign="top" width="50%" style="padding-right:14px;">
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:10px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.16em; color:#b8460a; text-transform:uppercase; padding-bottom:9px;">Shipping to</div>
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.72; color:#5a6b8c;">
                          <span style="color:#142548; font-weight:700;">{{ shipping_address.name }}</span><br>
                          {% if shipping_address.company != blank %}{{ shipping_address.company }}<br>{% endif %}
                          {{ shipping_address.address1 }}<br>
                          {% if shipping_address.address2 != blank %}{{ shipping_address.address2 }}<br>{% endif %}
                          {{ shipping_address.city }} {{ shipping_address.province_code }} {{ shipping_address.zip }}<br>
                          {{ shipping_address.country }}
                        </div>
                      </td>
                      <td class="stack-gap" style="font-size:0; line-height:0; height:0;">&nbsp;</td>
                    {%- endif %}
                    {%- if billing_address %}
                      <td class="stack" valign="top" width="50%">
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:10px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.16em; color:#b8460a; text-transform:uppercase; padding-bottom:9px;">Billed to</div>
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.72; color:#5a6b8c;">
                          <span style="color:#142548; font-weight:700;">{{ billing_address.name }}</span><br>
                          {% if billing_address.company != blank %}{{ billing_address.company }}<br>{% endif %}
                          {{ billing_address.address1 }}<br>
                          {% if billing_address.address2 != blank %}{{ billing_address.address2 }}<br>{% endif %}
                          {{ billing_address.city }} {{ billing_address.province_code }} {{ billing_address.zip }}<br>
                          {{ billing_address.country }}
                        </div>
                      </td>
                    {%- endif %}
                  </tr>
                </table>

                {%- comment -%}
                  Payment method and shipping method, the two fields Shopify's
                  own template carries under Customer information. They are the
                  detail people check when reconciling a statement or querying
                  which service they paid for, so they stay.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="padding-top:24px;">
                  <tr>
                    <td class="stack" valign="top" width="50%" style="padding-right:14px;">
                      <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:10px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.16em; color:#b8460a; text-transform:uppercase; padding-bottom:9px;">Payment</div>
                      <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.72; color:#5a6b8c;">
                        {%- for transaction in transactions -%}
                          {%- if transaction.status == 'success' and transaction.kind != 'refund' and transaction.kind != 'void' -%}
                            {%- if transaction.payment_details.credit_card_company -%}
                              {{ transaction.payment_details.credit_card_company }} ending in {{ transaction.payment_details.credit_card_last_four }}<br>
                            {%- else -%}
                              {{ transaction.gateway_display_name | default: transaction.gateway }}<br>
                            {%- endif -%}
                          {%- endif -%}
                        {%- endfor -%}
                      </div>
                    </td>
                    <td class="stack-gap" style="font-size:0; line-height:0; height:0;">&nbsp;</td>
                    {%- if requires_shipping and shipping_method %}
                      <td class="stack" valign="top" width="50%">
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:10px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.16em; color:#b8460a; text-transform:uppercase; padding-bottom:9px;">Shipping method</div>
                        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.72; color:#5a6b8c;">
                          {{ shipping_method.title }}
                        </div>
                      </td>
                    {%- endif %}
                  </tr>
                </table>

                {%- comment -%}
                  The line Shopify's original closes on. It belongs here rather
                  than in the footer: this is where someone finishes reading the
                  detail and finds a discrepancy.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <div style="border-top:1px solid #e7ecf4; margin-top:24px; padding-top:18px; font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.6; color:#5a6b8c;">
                  Any questions? Reply to this email or contact us at
                  <a href="mailto:info@hooknloop.com.au?subject=Order%20{{ order_name | url_encode }}" style="color:#b8460a; font-weight:700; text-decoration:none;">info@hooknloop.com.au</a>.
                </div>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <!-- ══ FOOTER ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
          {%- comment -%}
            The footer carries the contact details now, so it is built to be
            used rather than skimmed past. A trade buyer chasing an order wants
            a phone number, not a help centre — so the number is the largest
            thing here, set in mono at heading size and wired as a tel: link so
            it dials on a phone. The email sits under it as the written-record
            alternative for anyone forwarding to accounts.

            The reversed logo anchors it, and the tagline sits under the mark
            rather than in a second column — the two-column version left a
            narrow measure that broke the phone number across two lines.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <tr>
            <td style="background:#142548; padding:32px 30px;" class="px">

              {%- comment -%}
                The reversed logo, not the blue one. hnl-email-logo-footer.png
                is the white mark with the orange "n" — the blue version would
                vanish on navy exactly as it did in the masthead.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0975/4509/3489/files/hnl-email-logo-footer.png?v=1786003221"
                   alt="HooknLoop" width="164" height="29"
                   style="display:block; width:164px; height:29px; border:0;">

              <div style="font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.62; color:#8194b5; padding-top:14px; max-width:430px;">
                Australian hook &amp; loop specialists — tapes, strips, dots and fasteners, stocked and dispatched locally.
              </div>

              <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.13); margin-top:22px; padding-top:22px;">

                {%- comment -%}
                  Phone and email sit on one line at a size that cannot wrap.
                  The previous version set the number at 19px inside a 55%
                  column, which broke it across two lines mid-number — a phone
                  number that wraps is a phone number nobody dials.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:10px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.16em; color:#f0842a; text-transform:uppercase; padding-bottom:12px;">Need a hand?</div>

                <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
                  <tr>
                    <td class="stack" valign="middle" style="white-space:nowrap; padding-right:18px;">
                      <a href="tel:+61340616287" style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:#ffffff; text-decoration:none; white-space:nowrap;">+61&nbsp;3&nbsp;4061&nbsp;6287</a>
                    </td>
                    <td class="stack-gap" style="font-size:0; line-height:0; height:0;">&nbsp;</td>
                    <td class="stack" valign="middle" align="right" style="white-space:nowrap;">
                      <a href="mailto:info@hooknloop.com.au?subject=Order%20{{ order_name | url_encode }}" style="font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#c9d3e6; text-decoration:none; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(201,211,230,0.38); white-space:nowrap;">info@hooknloop.com.au</a>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </table>

              </div>

              <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.13); margin-top:22px; padding-top:16px;">
                <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
                  <tr>
                    <td align="left">
                      <a href="{{ shop.url }}" style="font-family:'DM Sans','Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; font-weight:700; color:#ffffff; text-decoration:none;">hooknloop.com.au</a>
                    </td>
                    <td align="right" style="font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,'Liberation Mono',monospace; font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; color:#8194b5; white-space:nowrap;">
                      Order {{ order_name }}
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </table>
              </div>

            </td>
          </tr>

        </table>

      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

</body>
</html>
